==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US|caught-cot}} {{IPA|/ɑθɛnˈtɪsɪti/|/ɑθənˈtɪsɪti/|[ɑθɛnˈtɪsɪɾi]|[ɑθənˈtɪsɪɾi]|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
{{suffix|authentic|ity|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|authenticities}}

# The quality of being [[genuine]] or not corrupted from the original.
#: ''I hereby certify the '''authenticity''' of this copy.''
# Truthfulness of origins, attributions, commitments, sincerity, and intentions.
#: ''The '''authenticity''' of this painting is questionable.''
# {{label|en|obsolete}} The quality of being [[authentic]] (of established [[authority]]).

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|quality of being genuine}} {{l|en|genuineness}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|quality of not being genuine}} {{l|en|phoniness}}; [[forgery]]; [[fakeness]]; [[bogosity]]

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|authentically}}
* {{l|en|authenticism}}

